Replace all backend-to-TUI state transfer with backend-owned canonical objects wrapped in runtime::UnlockedData<T>, registered through app::frontend::FrontEnd and consumed through frontend projection members owned by TuiFrontEnd. Follow the existing ModelSelection and SessionStats implementations: backend writes notify only dirtiness; the tui-thread calls foo_refresh(), copies canonical data under the appropriate read lock, derives presentation values, and independently consumes accumulated changed flags. RefreshResult<T> supports display strings and typed values where consumers require numeric or structured data. The backend must never write TUI caches, construct TUI presentation objects, or require the TUI to pull from Session or other backend implementation objects.

Complete decoupling means separating outgoing user actions from incoming state. Actions remain permissioned backend requests with explicit success/error/control outcomes; resulting observable state arrives exclusively through the canonical-data path. Ordered events and interactive decisions must retain their ordering, authority and delivery guarantees through explicitly designed frontend-neutral boundaries, not survive as disguised state-transfer bypasses. Session replacement and stale asynchronous work must be handled by coherent identity/generation rules, not by applying a bulk UI snapshot.

At completion no Snapshot object is used to transfer backend data to the TUI: remove TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot, TuiSubmitResult::state_snapshot and other transported snapshot contracts, including narrow startup/trust/branch/subagent state payloads where they cross this boundary. Do not merely rename snapshot bundles or wrap the old runtime snapshot wholesale in UnlockedData. Backend-internal snapshots and frontend-internal copied snapshots/render/editor state may remain: the latter are fundamental to this design, but must be produced locally from frontend projections rather than delivered by backend callbacks. Preserve all existing working terminal behavior, backend permissions and session authority, and non-TUI frontends. Complete the migration in buildable, independently verified slices, deleting each obsolete transfer path as its replacement is enabled.
